  "body": "## Scope and dependency\n\nDepends on draft PR #346 at 892038c7d7ec64082b39917127f67748e6d1dca7. Fixes the current-token authentication-to-event window using the existing api_token row, not a new session or event domain.\n\nAuthentication captures an opaque request-local token ID, original party and SHA-256 credential fingerprint. The event GET/new-command/replay transaction locks and revalidates that row with FOR SHARE and holds it through commit. Deactivation, deletion, rotation, party rebinding, reset-purpose conversion and absent/copied witnesses fail closed. Fingerprints use constEq and witness Show is redacted. Synthetic fixture users and the existing notification-reviewer projection explicitly carry no witness. Other domain authorization semantics stay unchanged.\n\n## Requirements and formal gate\n\nEO-003 / EO-045 / EO-051 / EO-055 map to SessionFence.CurrentBoundSession. Full pinned TLC/Alloy verification passed before production edits. SessionFence checked 12,685 generated / 1,153 distinct states, depth 5, with 32 token records, two actors and read/new/replay. Six negative configurations each violated the required invariant; all sixteen negative controls in the full runner were detected. Alloy had a SAT scenario and eight UNSAT assertions within existing scopes. This is bounded current-validity analysis, not permanent revocation or an unbounded proof.\n\n## Verified evidence\n\n- Before implementation: the new captured-session regression failed, while all 18 existing HTTP examples passed.\n- Final npm run test:event-operations-http: 36 examples, zero failures against fresh PostgreSQL 16; 21 real HTTP examples plus 15 direct handler/session/database cases. Includes real post-authentication HTTP barriers, unchanged receipts/audit/state, both observed PostgreSQL lock orders, RC/RR/Serializable, cancellation and sanitized query-failure recovery.\n- npm run quality:repo: PASS, including 21 CI tests. Final staged heuristic audit passed with zero critical/errors and 354 advisory warnings; this is separate from TLC/Alloy.\n- Runner safety: 3/3 PASS. Changed YAML, shell syntax, documentation links and whitespace checks passed. Temporary test containers were removed.\n- Full backend compatibility build is NOT yet verified. The initial optimized rebuild was interrupted at module 52/209 with exit 130; the normal Stack fast-profile replacement remains running. No full backend test run or green hosted CI is claimed.\n\n## Schema, rollback and privacy\n\nNo table/column migration, deployed checksum change, extra authentication route, wire DTO or generated-client change. Rejected sessions return a fixed authentication-style 401 before event SQL. Existing scopes and receipt privacy remain required. Rollback keeps event operations disabled and reverts the Haskell context/handler/fixture increment coherently; never enable the old unfenced handler. CI requirements and production optimization are unchanged.\n\n## Remaining gates\n\nExplicitly reactivating the SAME credential still reauthorizes it; permanent revocation requires rotation or leaving old tokens inactive. Global role/catalog changes, other domain transactions, token storage/lifetime policy, full mkApp/schema rehearsal, mobile/browser/offline flows and the rest of the event product remain pending. Parent hosted failures are not waived. No merge, auto-merge, production deployment/migration/credential activation or real-money action.\n\nExact commands, bounds, implementation mapping and limitations: docs/event-operations/pr-09-session-fence.md and docs/event-operations/session-fence-contract.md.",
